"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs (GS) and Bank of America (BAC) explicitly disclose that divergent stakeholder views on climate change create reputational risks, where any action or inaction may be perceived negatively. GS states that due to these divergent views, it faces increased risk of negative perception by some stakeholders, which could adversely affect its business and reputation, and specifically notes potential harm to employee recruitment and retention. BAC makes a nearly identical disclosure, stating that due to divergent views, it is at increased risk that its actions or lack thereof regarding climate change will be perceived negatively, impacting reputation and business. BAC’s disclosure focuses on legal, compliance, and reputational harm from negative public sentiment and regulatory scrutiny, while GS emphasizes the operational impact on reputation and hiring.",
