"comparison": "Citi (C) and Goldman Sachs (GS) both identify risks arising from stakeholder views on climate change, though they frame the consequences differently. GS explicitly links divergent stakeholder views to the risk of negative perception of its actions or inaction, which could harm its reputation and business. Citi discloses that it may face challenges and scrutiny from stakeholders with varied views on climate change that may impact its ability to conduct certain business, and separately notes that perceived overstatements of environmental benefits could result in reputational harm and legal/regulatory actions. Both companies acknowledge that the transition to a low-carbon economy involves complex stakeholder dynamics that pose reputational and operational risks.",
